FIX ASSETS (INFIX)
==================

Source PNG images for Neo Geo FIX layer tiles (S1 ROM).

  Format:   PNG, indexed palette (mode P), max 15 colours
  Colours:  palette index 0 = transparent; indices 1-15 = visible colours
  Size:     multiples of 8x8 pixels (each 8x8 block = one FIX tile)
  Naming:   0.png, 1.png, 2.png ... (romdbfiximport.py imports all PNGs found)

The FIX layer is used for text overlays, HUDs, score displays, and static
elements that are drawn on top of the sprite layer.

Pipeline:
  romdbfiximport.py  →  imagefix table in neorom.db
  fixtiles.py        →  777-s1.s1 (128 KB, hardware format)

fixtiles.py build order:
  1. Seed from sfix.sfix (standard NeoGeo system fonts)
  2. Preserve all non-empty tiles from existing 777-s1.s1
  3. Write infix PNG tiles into empty slots (tile 256+)

Run: make sfix  (or make srom)   →  roms/neogeosdk/777-s1.s1

Convert an RGB image to indexed palette (Pillow):
  from PIL import Image
  img = Image.open("source.png").quantize(colors=15)
  img.save("infix/0.png")
